Nothing changed for #3 this run, so I backed it off again until 2026-12-05.

The new comment from jodydadescott only removed the stale `Blocked-by: #36` line. What actually holds this issue is a missing label: #3 still doesn't have `looper:workflows`, and a member has to add it. Until it's there, `.github/workflows/release.yml` can't be pushed, and no image or GitHub release can be published.

The checkpoint tool ran into a git identity error ("Author identity unknown"), so its commit came out empty, but the wait itself was recorded. The checkout had no changes, so nothing was lost.

When the label is added, that wakes the issue, and the next run will:
1. Commit and land `release.yml`.
2. Publish v0.1.0, v0.1.1 and v0.2.0 through v0.2.4 with the workflow's publish option, handling the GitHub releases that already exist.
3. Make the `stratum` package public.
4. Do a dry run of the next patch on each line, then close the issue.
